    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30206" root="علج" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلُوجٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلُوكٌ</span> (O, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلُوكٌ</span>, meaning <i>A
thing that is eaten</i> [or <i>chewed</i>]: (O:) so in the
phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا عَلُوجُ صِدْقٍ</span> [<i>This is an excellent thing
that is chewed</i>]. (O, K.) See also 5.

